<title>LITHUANIA: Yield on 6-mth Lithuanian T-bills dips at auction.</title>
<headline>Yield on 6-mth Lithuanian T-bills dips at auction.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on six-month Lithuanian Treasury bills dipped to 12.94 percent at auction on Tuesday from 14.50 percent at the last sale of six month paper, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Amounts are in millions of litas  MATURITY    AV YIELD  (LAST TIME)   MIN/MAX   ISSUE  BID   SOLD</p>
<p> 182-day	12.94	14.50     10.80/14.48  30   48.896  30</p>
<p>Settlement date for today's auction is October 18 and the bills mature on April 18, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Tallinn Newsroom +372 630 8400</p>
</text>
